  "prompt": "=== Chain-of-thought analysis prompt ===\nYou are a software requirements analyst preparing a UML state machine model.\n\nAnalyze the requirement and extract only the modeling facts needed for a state transition diagram. Keep the analysis concise and evidence-based.\n\nReturn the analysis using exactly these headings:\nStates:\nInitial state:\nFinal states:\nEvents or conditions:\nTransitions:\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n\nDo not write PlantUML in this step.\n\nRequirement:\nSafehome Security Function — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall check if everything is working upon power-on.\n2. The system shall stop if there is a problem during startup.\n3. The system shall become ready to use if everything is fine during startup.\n4. The system shall allow the user to reset it when it is ready to use.\n5. The system shall allow the user to activate it when it is ready to use.\n6. The system shall allow the user to turn it off when it is ready to use.\n7. The system shall start monitoring if it is activated.\n8. The system shall start the alarm and send alerts if a sensor is triggered during monitoring.\n9. The system shall continue monitoring if it turns out to be a false alarm or the time ends.\n10. The system shall stop and return to normal when the user enters the password at any time.\n\n=== Chain-of-thought analysis response ===\nStates:\n- Powering On\n- Startup Check\n- Ready To Use\n- Monitoring\n- Alarm Activated\n- Normal\n\nInitial state:\nPowering On\n\nFinal states:\nNormal\n\nEvents or conditions:\n- Power-On\n- Startup Complete (No Problems)\n- Reset Requested by User\n- Activation Requested by User\n- Deactivation Requested by User\n- Sensor Triggered\n- False Alarm Confirmed\n- Time Ends\n- Password Entered\n\nTransitions:\n1. From Powering On to Startup Check on Power-On.\n2. From Startup Check to Ready To Use if Startup Complete (No Problems).\n3. From Ready To Use to Monitoring on Activation Requested by User.\n4. From Monitoring to Alarm Activated on Sensor Triggered.\n5. From Alarm Activated to Monitoring on False Alarm Confirmed or Time Ends.\n6. From Monitoring, Alarm Activated, and Ready To Use to Normal on Password Entered.\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n- The requirement does not specify the exact sequence of events after a false alarm is confirmed or if the time ends in the monitoring state.\n- It is unclear what happens when the system returns to the \"Normal\" state other than waiting for another event.\n\n=== PlantUML generation prompt ===\nYou are a UML modeling expert.\n\nConvert the requirement and the structured analysis into one UML state transition diagram in PlantUML format.\n\nOutput Rules:\n- Generate ONLY valid PlantUML code.\n- Start with @startuml and end with @enduml.\n- Use [*] for exactly one initial transition.\n- Include at least one final transition to [*].\n- Use clear transition labels when requirement evidence exists.\n- Do not include explanations, analysis, or markdown fences.\n\nRequirement:\nSafehome Security Function — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall check if everything is working upon power-on.\n2. The system shall stop if there is a problem during startup.\n3. The system shall become ready to use if everything is fine during startup.\n4. The system shall allow the user to reset it when it is ready to use.\n5. The system shall allow the user to activate it when it is ready to use.\n6. The system shall allow the user to turn it off when it is ready to use.\n7. The system shall start monitoring if it is activated.\n8. The system shall start the alarm and send alerts if a sensor is triggered during monitoring.\n9. The system shall continue monitoring if it turns out to be a false alarm or the time ends.\n10. The system shall stop and return to normal when the user enters the password at any time.\n\nStructured analysis from step 1:\nStates:\n- Powering On\n- Startup Check\n- Ready To Use\n- Monitoring\n- Alarm Activated\n- Normal\n\nInitial state:\nPowering On\n\nFinal states:\nNormal\n\nEvents or conditions:\n- Power-On\n- Startup Complete (No Problems)\n- Reset Requested by User\n- Activation Requested by User\n- Deactivation Requested by User\n- Sensor Triggered\n- False Alarm Confirmed\n- Time Ends\n- Password Entered\n\nTransitions:\n1. From Powering On to Startup Check on Power-On.\n2. From Startup Check to Ready To Use if Startup Complete (No Problems).\n3. From Ready To Use to Monitoring on Activation Requested by User.\n4. From Monitoring to Alarm Activated on Sensor Triggered.\n5. From Alarm Activated to Monitoring on False Alarm Confirmed or Time Ends.\n6. From Monitoring, Alarm Activated, and Ready To Use to Normal on Password Entered.\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n- The requirement does not specify the exact sequence of events after a false alarm is confirmed or if the time ends in the monitoring state.\n- It is unclear what happens when the system returns to the \"Normal\" state other than waiting for another event.\n\nNow return only the final PlantUML.\n",
